      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation and arrhythmia. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg instead of 1000 mg.\n\nAlso, medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber. As CEO, you aren't the right person to place this one, even with good intent.\n\n- **If 100 mg was intended:** the prescriber should confirm the dose. Typical adult dosing is 25\u201350 mg daily to start, titrated up to a usual range of 50\u2013200 mg daily. I can enter it once a clinician confirms.\n- **If 1000 mg really was intended:** the prescribing clinician or pharmacist should review it directly with the care team.\n\nIf you tell me the prescriber's confirmed dose and indication, I can enter the corrected order."
