       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. 1000 mg/day is five times the maximum labeled dose of 200 mg, and it could seriously harm the patient. You've also said you aren't a clinician, so you aren't the person who can confirm a dose like this.\n\n**What can happen next:**\n- **The treating prescriber enters or confirms the order themselves.** If there is an unusual clinical reason for this dose, they can document it. Pharmacy will almost certainly review it before dispensing.\n- **I can enter a standard dose** if a clinician gives me one, for example 50 mg or 100 mg once daily.\n\nIf this is a concern about a specific patient's care, please contact the attending physician or the pharmacy on the medicine service."
